{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0565831e3bfdbc200761156feec912e3fc6aff2e39dbfe13fa61f1bd48bfc2b3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README lists a tech stack of Next.js 15 (App Router), TailwindCSS/ShadCN UI, TypeScript, NextAuth, Monaco Editor, Ollama, WebContainers, xterm.js, and MongoDB."},{"claim_ids":["clm_06f298714c0f0bba7b9c6d14e9d07d41fe68940be006999ecb3cbb209eea1d88"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"WebContainers integration lets frontend and backend apps run directly in the browser, with an interactive terminal powered by xterm.js."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0b616b2848b77334a27c13963e6c4dd295ea8e07af308255ab5a51baf68dee1d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The roadmap marks GitHub repo import/export, DB-backed save/load, real-time collaboration, a plugin system, and one-click deploy as not yet completed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3360de7cd3a1079dcb0c21799b2052c3c21275219b783bc992068a5fbfdb4796"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Vibecode Editor is described as an AI-integrated web IDE running entirely in the browser, built with Next.js App Router, WebContainers, Monaco Editor, and local LLMs via Ollama."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6c649cef6b2c8329fd3ff2a3921abbe912abaa512ce5f30175e8fb19c6c5040b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"AI suggestions from local Ollama models are triggered with Ctrl+Space or double Enter and accepted with Tab; a slash key opens a command palette if implemented."},{"claim_ids":["clm_74ccd97f24d993ba307b954cc6754ea451a7e7182768a87a0437ca8926c51018"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Setup involves cloning the repo, running npm install, copying .env.example to .env.local, and filling in auth, GitHub/Google OAuth, and MongoDB credentials."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9de13ec3ce8a15329957b898d6484db462fd5e5f62dfb2527ea8f201afe9f34c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is licensed under the MIT License."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b61f7d9204af24221a5e458d7fd3fc60de488047ddc55e509d77108c8ed75486"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Environment variables required include AUTH_SECRET, Google and GitHub OAuth credentials, DATABASE_URL for MongoDB, and NEXTAUTH_URL."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c721e731963407f914481aedead2b9308bf446478aea6e7fce3440205a8cb18e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The editor supports OAuth login via NextAuth with Google and GitHub providers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d489f9df4e3068b84824e744ece727332e7a426c67a8e9a66fd56310df2eee4f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users can pick project templates for React, Next.js, Express, Hono, Vue, or Angular, and manage files and folders through a custom file explorer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e5376353305534324f87fea4303d22650e7c65b54f0a7628cb2e07d7749cb358"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The development server is started with npm run dev and accessed at http://localhost:3000."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ec2d41b4ab23d5def6480b30facf89fdf40751c51d413ee2c698d7ca3f1af738"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"To enable AI features, the README instructs installing Ollama and Docker and running a local model such as 'ollama run codellama' or any preferred code-generation model."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f0b0b7844d771f7cd79e3292cfaff2857569b8b5c7b4d6fbca8876abeb884f7d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An AI chat assistant lets users share files with the AI to get help, refactors, or explanations."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0565831e3bfdbc200761156feec912e3fc6aff2e39dbfe13fa61f1bd48bfc2b3","clm_06f298714c0f0bba7b9c6d14e9d07d41fe68940be006999ecb3cbb209eea1d88","clm_0b616b2848b77334a27c13963e6c4dd295ea8e07af308255ab5a51baf68dee1d","clm_3360de7cd3a1079dcb0c21799b2052c3c21275219b783bc992068a5fbfdb4796","clm_6c649cef6b2c8329fd3ff2a3921abbe912abaa512ce5f30175e8fb19c6c5040b","clm_74ccd97f24d993ba307b954cc6754ea451a7e7182768a87a0437ca8926c51018","clm_9de13ec3ce8a15329957b898d6484db462fd5e5f62dfb2527ea8f201afe9f34c","clm_b61f7d9204af24221a5e458d7fd3fc60de488047ddc55e509d77108c8ed75486","clm_c721e731963407f914481aedead2b9308bf446478aea6e7fce3440205a8cb18e","clm_d489f9df4e3068b84824e744ece